      "error_message": "AttributeError: 'bool' object has no attribute 'loop' — init_bridge accesses mc_config.autonomous.loop but autonomous is a bool",
      "file": "src/animetta/tools/minecraft/core/config.py, src/animetta/tools/minecraft/core/tools.py",
      "root_cause": "config.py:30 defines MinecraftConfig.autonomous as bool, but tools.py:47 accesses mc_config.autonomous.loop (treating it as an object with a .loop attribute). tools.yaml passes autonomous: true (a bool), so True.loop raises AttributeError on bridge init. Effect: the autonomous loop never starts, which means the entire Voyager-side (planner, skill learning loop, LLM-driven decisions) is dead code. mc-bot still works only because Survival Runner is invoked via direct LangChain tool calls (mc_survival_iron), NOT via the autonomous loop.",
      "fix": "Planned in OpenSpec change mc-bot-voyager-learning task T1: replace the broken autonomous.loop access with a MinecraftMode enum (learn/live/fallback) stored as config.mode. Not yet fixed — identified during brainstorming session, fix scheduled for implementation phase.",
