      "id": "bug-063",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-27T21:45:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "ReferenceError: require is not defined in ES module scope — bot/index.js node startup crash (bot stdout closed within 1s, bridge 'login timeout', 'Bridge not running')",
      "file": "src/animetta/tools/minecraft/bot/index.js",
      "root_cause": "T2 eval_code sandbox added `const vm = require('vm');` but bot/index.js is an ES module (package.json has \"type\": \"module\"). ESM does not support require(). Node crashed at startup so the bot process exited immediately — bridge saw stdout close, login timed out, and every command (spectate/eval_code) failed with 'Bridge not running'. This was a regression introduced by T2 that only surfaced when actually launching the bot end-to-end.",
      "fix": "Changed `const vm = require('vm');` to `import vm from 'vm';` (ESM import syntax). Verified node starts cleanly and bot logs in. Lesson: bot/index.js is ESM — always use import, never require.",
